        "width": 5869,
        "height": 3832,
        "date": "2019-02-27 07:49:37",
        "description": "The San Joaquin cemetery also known as \"Campo Santo\" or mortuary chapel, is a Roman Catholic cemetery located in the Municipality of San Joaquin, Iloilo, Philippines. The cemetery is perhaps the grandest and best preserved in the entire Province of Iloilo. The cemetery was built during the Spanish-colonial period of the Philippines, the San Joaquin cemetery was initiated in 1892 by Fray Mariano Vamba, the last Augustinian parish priest of the town. A statue of Jesus with his arms outstretched stands on top of a Baroque-style gate, and on each side of Christ, two columns with angelic figures are poised as guards. In addition, sculpted heads of two cherubs and a skull representing death marks the entrance of the cemetery. After entering the gate, visitors are by the mortuary chapel or “Campo Santo,” decorated with stone carvings of floral and leaf patterns.",
