        "description": "The CAMPO SANTO de San Joaquin is located along the main highway in San Joaquin Town around 57 kilometers away from Iloilo City, which is situated in the southern part of Iloilo and one of the oldest cemetery in Panay Island. The construction of San Joaquin Cemetery was commenced by Fray Mariano Vamba, the last Augustinian parish priest of the town in 1892. A statue of Jesus with his arms outstretched stands on top of a baroque style gate, and on each side of Christ, two columns with angelic figures are poised as guards. In addition, sculpted heads of two cherubs and a skull representing death marks the entrance of the cemetery. Twenty stone steps after entering the gate and you will be greeted by the Baroque designed mortuary chapel standing on the center.",
